/*
  MageRide Driver — iOS shell strings (C085 driver-ios-shell). English, the development region.

  SCOPE. Only what the SHELL renders: the tab bar, the offline banner, the update gate, the map
  affordances and the handful of actions and errors every screen group shares. A screen group's own
  copy belongs to that component (C086-C093) and is added to all three files together.

  KEYS ARE C067'S. The same key names as `apps/driver-android/src/main/res/values…/strings.xml`, so
  a screen group porting its Android copy has a one-to-one mapping and a divergence between the two
  apps is a diff rather than an archaeology exercise. The VALUES are the same translations.

  THE RULE (CLAUDE.md). Every user-facing string is Si + Ta + En and nothing is hard-coded in a
  View. `LocalizationTests` fails the build if a key exists here and not in si/ta, if a translation
  is left equal to its English, or if a format specifier does not survive translation.

  NOT HERE. iOS has no notification channel a user can silence one-by-one and no ongoing
  foreground-service notification, so C067's `push_channel_*` and `location_notification_*` keys
  have no renderer on this platform (D2' §C: the channel is Android's, the blue location indicator
  is the system's and carries no app text). The location copy a driver DOES read on iOS is the
  purpose strings, which live in `InfoPlist.strings` beside this file.
*/

