  KEYS ARE C070'S. Same key names and the same translations as
  `apps/driver-android/src/main/res/values…/strings.xml`, so a divergence between the two driver
  apps is a diff rather than an archaeology exercise. `%1$s` becomes `%1$@`, which is the only
  systematic difference — see cluster 2's note above.

  THREE KEYS ARE NEW HERE, and each is something this platform draws and Android does not.
  `offer_countdown` is the ring's VoiceOver label — the Android twin's ring is a
  `CircularProgressIndicator` with the seconds as a sibling `Text`, which a screen reader already
  reads, while this one is a drawn shape and announces itself. `ride_call_unavailable` is the CallKit
